course: dictionary
lesson: 1574
title: Charity: one word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A charity is a group or organisation that collects money and help for people or animals in need. «A charity is a group that helps people or animals.» The clues are the group and the help, so this is the meaning to use.
explain: Charity can also mean giving. «To donate is to give money to help.» When you give money, food or help to people who need it, you are doing charity. In school, pupils raise money for charity with cake sales and fun runs.
explain: Charity can also mean kindness in judging other people. Look at the words around it to decide which meaning fits. Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A charity is an organisation that collects money and help for people or animals in need.
fact: Charity means giving money, food or help to people who need it.
fact: Charity can also mean kindness in judging other people, so being fair and kind when you judge someone.
fact: «CAFOD is the charity of the Catholic Church in England and Wales.»
fact: Useful phrases: give to charity, raise money for charity, charity shop, charity event.
exercise: «A charity is a group that helps people or animals.» What is a charity? | A shop that sells only cakes | *An organisation that collects money and help for people or animals in need | A school for dogs
exercise: «Coins thrown into a wishing fountain are usually collected for charity.» What does charity show here? | *The coins are collected to help people who need it | The coins are kept by whoever threw them in | The coins are turned into a wishing well
exercise: Pupils raise money for charity with a cake sale. What does charity mean here? | Running very fast | A kind of fancy cake | *Giving money to help people in need | Being fair when judging others
test: Which word means to give money to help? | shop | *donate | charity | fountain
test: Mia's teacher marks her work fairly and kindly, without judging her harshly. Which meaning of charity fits best? | *Kindness in judging other people | A dressing-up day at school | A group that runs fun runs for pupils | Money given to a fountain
exam: Which word means the same as charities in «Many faiths run charities for children without parents»? | A game played in the playground | A shop for children's shoes | *Organisations that help children | A school trip
